WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.947 --> 00:00:16.089
man from the hunting party turned to Vinnie and the young boy.

2
00:00:16.109 --> 00:00:19.571
"Sequoia, we are leaving," he said.

3
00:00:19.591 --> 00:00:22.193
"Will they give us cattle?"

4
00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:23.494
asked Sequoia.

5
00:00:24.635 --> 00:00:26.956
The man nodded and turned his horse around.

6
00:00:28.157 --> 00:00:29.098
The boy followed.

7
00:00:29.118 --> 00:00:32.080
"What are you doing, Frank?"

8
00:00:32.528 --> 00:00:33.188
Vinnie asked.

9
00:00:34.549 --> 00:00:37.389
The cowboys were taking some of the cows from the herd.

10
00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:41.711
"We're giving cattle to the Cherokee," replied Frank.

11
00:00:41.731 --> 00:00:43.831
"They are very hungry.

12
00:00:44.852 --> 00:00:46.472
These cattle will keep them alive.

13
00:00:47.452 --> 00:00:49.813
Plus, we must have peace between us."

14
00:00:51.614 --> 00:00:54.434
Vinnie watched the Cherokee ride off with the cattle.

15
00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:57.835
"What if you didn't give them anything?"

16
00:00:58.696 --> 00:00:59.356
Vinnie asked.

17
00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:05.303
Frank got back on his horse and said, "They probably would have attacked."

18
00:01:06.444 --> 00:01:07.305
Vinnie shivered.

19
00:01:09.266 --> 00:01:12.048
Cookie got back onto the wagon beside Mandy.

20
00:01:12.068 --> 00:01:14.469
"Is everything okay?"

21
00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:15.490
she asked.

22
00:01:16.491 --> 00:01:19.112
"There's nothing to worry about," said Cookie.

23
00:01:20.393 --> 00:01:23.095
The cowboys continued along the Chisholm Trail.

24
00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:27.398
They rode for hours, and Mandy was getting tired.

25
00:01:27.418 --> 00:01:31.933
"We're at the end of the trail now," Cookie said to Mandy.

26
00:01:33.214 --> 00:01:34.295
He pointed ahead.

27
00:01:35.516 --> 00:01:38.499
Mandy could see some buildings and men on horses.

28
00:01:38.519 --> 00:01:41.362
"What is that place called?"

29
00:01:41.902 --> 00:01:42.423
she asked.

30
00:01:42.443 --> 00:01:46.366
"That's Dodge City," Cookie answered.

31
00:01:47.427 --> 00:01:49.009
Frank rode up to the wagon.

32
00:01:49.029 --> 00:01:52.832
"Why don't you take the kids to the hotel, Cookie?

33
00:01:54.153 --> 00:01:55.735
We'll get the cattle to the market."

34
00:01:57.056 --> 00:02:01.820
Cookie urged the wagon's horses forward, and Vinnie followed close behind.

35
00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:04.182
"See you at the hotel!"

36
00:02:04.483 --> 00:02:08.726
called Frank as he led the cowboys in another direction.

37
00:02:09.927 --> 00:02:12.469
Cookie and the kids went to the center of town.

38
00:02:14.031 --> 00:02:18.575
Dodge City was muddy and noisy, and cowboys were everywhere.

39
00:02:19.816 --> 00:02:21.617
Their faces were different colors.

40
00:02:22.818 --> 00:02:24.520
They were dressed in different ways.

41
00:02:25.548 --> 00:02:29.771
But they were alike in one way—they all were dusty and dirty.

42
00:02:30.992 --> 00:02:34.834
The men laughed loudly and seemed to be having a good time.

43
00:02:36.115 --> 00:02:39.578
Cookie stopped his horses in front of a large wooden building.

44
00:02:40.918 --> 00:02:43.340
The entrance had swinging wooden doors.

45
00:02:44.961 --> 00:02:48.063
The children could hear a piano and lots of shouting.

46
00:02:48.083 --> 00:02:51.526
"What's this place?"

47
00:02:52.706 --> 00:02:54.848
asked Vinnie, patting his horse's neck.

48
00:02:56.484 --> 00:03:00.588
Suddenly, a man stumbled backward through the swinging doors.

49
00:03:01.769 --> 00:03:03.450
He landed in the muddy street.

50
00:03:04.611 --> 00:03:07.073
Another man came out shaking his fist.

51
00:03:07.093 --> 00:03:10.556
"This is the saloon," said Cookie.

52
00:03:10.576 --> 00:03:12.898
"Not a place for children."

53
00:03:14.239 --> 00:03:16.861
Cookie took them across the street to the hotel.

54
00:03:18.062 --> 00:03:23.226
Inside, families were eating at tables and people were playing cards.

55
00:03:23.246 --> 00:03:28.901
"Nellie?" Cookie called to a pretty young woman wearing an apron.

56
00:03:28.921 --> 00:03:32.662
"Howdy," she said in a friendly voice.

57
00:03:32.682 --> 00:03:36.623
"Glad to see you're back from the trail safely."

58
00:03:36.643 --> 00:03:40.244
"Thanks, Nellie," said Cookie.

59
00:03:41.284 --> 00:03:42.785
He introduced the children.

60
00:03:42.805 --> 00:03:45.405
"Keep an eye on them for me.

61
00:03:46.746 --> 00:03:48.686
I'm going to the saloon for a little drink."

62
00:03:50.487 --> 00:03:56.546
"Hey, kids, we're about to have a square dance in the back room," said Nellie.

63
00:03:56.567 --> 00:03:57.459
"Do you want to dance?"
